  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light of intensity <math><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;is incident on a parallel glass-slab at the point <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and it undergoes partial reflection and refraction as shown in the figure. At each reflection,&nbsp;<math><mn>25</mn><mi>%</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math>of the incident energy is reflected and the rest is transmitted. If the rays <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>A</mi><mi>&#8242;</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>&#8242;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math>undergo interference, then the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></math> is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0103_97c5588b7696.png\" style=\"width: 225px; height: 156px;\" />"
  },
